// Lithuanian (lt) — Baltic, Latin script. Referee: wikipron lit_latn_narrow (HUMAN, CUNY-CL/wikipron, 15,513 words),
// a LARGE narrow-phonetic set. `segmentJoin` strips its per-phone spaces. Lithuanian STRESS is lexical + pitch-accented
// (unpredictable from spelling), and vowel LENGTH + the stressed ɑː/æː quality are stress-conditioned — so we emit the
// phonemic short quality and FOLD: the referee's ¹/² pitch marks, length (ː ˑ), and the stressed/allophonic vowel
// qualities (ɑ→ɐ, æ→ɛ, ɔ→o loan-⟨o⟩, u-family→ʊ). The BACKBONE already strips the fronting ̟. The PALATALIZATION (ʲ),
// every consonant place, and the segment skeleton ARE compared directly — that is the real signal here. See
// docs/investigations/lt_bringup_investigation.md.
